#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Graph &rarr; Hamiltonian {#graph-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Graf &rarr; Hamiltonian {#graph-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, map the problem onto a quantum circuit that is suited for the QAOA. Details on this process can be found in the [introductory QAOA tutorial](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm).\n"
msgstr "Pertama, petakan masalah ke atas Circuit kuantum yang sesuai untuk QAOA. Butiran mengenai proses ini boleh didapati dalam [tutorial QAOA pengenalan](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/8b864d32-9483-45ea-831f-60488e330adb-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/8b864d32-9483-45ea-831f-60488e330adb-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "SWAP strategy with the SAT initial mapping {#swap-strategy-with-the-sat-initial-mapping}"
msgstr "Strategi SWAP dengan pemetaan awal SAT {#swap-strategy-with-the-sat-initial-mapping}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will demonstrate how to build and optimize QAOA circuits using the **SWAP strategy with SAT initial mapping**, a specifically designed transpiler pass for QAOA applied to quadratic problems.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan menunjukkan cara membina dan mengoptimumkan Circuit QAOA menggunakan **strategi SWAP dengan pemetaan awal SAT**, sebuah pas Transpiler yang direka khas untuk QAOA yang digunakan pada masalah kuadratik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this example, we choose a SWAP insertion strategy for blocks of commuting two-qubit gates, which applies layers of SWAP gates that are simultaneously executable on the coupling map. This strategy is presented in [\\[1\\]](#references) and is passed into `Commuting2qGateRouter`, which is exposed as a standardized Qiskit transpiler pass (see [`Commuting2qGateRouter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Commuting2qGateRouter)). We use a line swap strategy in this example.\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh ini, kita memilih strategi penyisipan SWAP untuk blok gate dua-qubit yang berkomutatif, yang menerapkan lapisan gate SWAP yang boleh dilaksanakan serentak pada peta gandingan. Strategi ini dibentangkan dalam [\\[1\\]](#references) dan dimasukkan ke dalam `Commuting2qGateRouter`, yang didedahkan sebagai pas Transpiler Qiskit yang distandardkan (lihat [`Commuting2qGateRouter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Commuting2qGateRouter)). Kita menggunakan strategi swap garisan dalam contoh ini.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remap the graph using a SAT mapper {#remap-the-graph-using-a-sat-mapper}"
msgstr "Petakan semula graf menggunakan SAT mapper {#remap-the-graph-using-a-sat-mapper}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Even when a circuit consists of commuting gates (this is the case for the QAOA circuit, but also for Trotterized simulations of Ising Hamiltonians), finding a good initial mapping is a challenging task. When we use the SAT-based approach presented in [\\[2\\]](#references), we can discover effective initial mappings for circuits with commuting gates, resulting in a significant reduction in the number of required SWAP layers. This approach has been demonstrated to scale to up to *500 qubits*, as illustrated in the paper.\n"
msgstr "Walaupun apabila Circuit terdiri daripada gate yang berkomutatif (ini adalah kes untuk Circuit QAOA, tetapi juga untuk simulasi Trotterisasi Hamiltonian Ising), mencari pemetaan awal yang baik adalah tugas yang mencabar. Apabila kita menggunakan pendekatan berasaskan SAT yang dibentangkan dalam [\\[2\\]](#references), kita boleh menemui pemetaan awal yang berkesan untuk Circuit dengan gate yang berkomutatif, menghasilkan pengurangan ketara dalam bilangan lapisan SWAP yang diperlukan. Pendekatan ini telah ditunjukkan untuk berskala sehingga *500 qubit*, seperti yang digambarkan dalam kertas tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code demonstrates how to use the `SATMapper` from Matsuo et al. to remap the graph. This process allows the problem to be mapped to a more optimal initial state for a specified SWAP strategy, resulting in a significant reduction in the number of SWAP layers required to execute the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kod berikut menunjukkan cara menggunakan `SATMapper` daripada Matsuo et al. untuk memetakan semula graf. Proses ini membolehkan masalah dipetakan ke keadaan awal yang lebih optimum untuk strategi SWAP yang ditentukan, menghasilkan pengurangan ketara dalam bilangan lapisan SWAP yang diperlukan untuk melaksanakan Circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In `SATMapper`, the problem of finding a good initial mapping is formulated as a SAT problem. A SAT solver is used to find such an initial mapping for the QAOA circuit. `python-sat` (`pysat` for short) is a Python library for a SAT solver, and we will use it to solve the SAT problem in this example.\n"
msgstr "Dalam `SATMapper`, masalah mencari pemetaan awal yang baik diformulasikan sebagai masalah SAT. Penyelesai SAT digunakan untuk mencari pemetaan awal sedemikian untuk Circuit QAOA. `python-sat` (singkatannya `pysat`) adalah pustaka Python untuk penyelesai SAT, dan kita akan menggunakannya untuk menyelesaikan masalah SAT dalam contoh ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/e689e09e-6ca7-4154-8602-d1d954ebe80b-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/e689e09e-6ca7-4154-8602-d1d954ebe80b-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a QAOA circuit with the SWAP strategy and the SAT mapping {#build-a-qaoa-circuit-with-the-swap-strategy-and-the-sat-mapping}"
msgstr "Bina Circuit QAOA dengan strategi SWAP dan pemetaan SAT {#build-a-qaoa-circuit-with-the-swap-strategy-and-the-sat-mapping}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We only want to apply the SWAP strategies to the cost operator layer, so we start by creating the isolated block that we will later transform and append to the final QAOA circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kita hanya mahu menerapkan strategi SWAP pada lapisan operator kos, jadi kita mulakan dengan mencipta blok terpencil yang kemudiannya akan kita transformasi dan tambahkan ke Circuit QAOA akhir.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this, we can use the [`QAOAAnsatz`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.QAOAAnsatz) class from Qiskit. We input an empty circuit to the `initial_state` and `mixer_operator` fields to make sure we are building an isolated cost operator layer.\n"
"We also define the `edge_coloring` map so that RZZ gates are positioned next to SWAP gates. This strategic placement allows us to exploit CX cancellations, optimizing the circuit for better performance.\n"
"This process is executed within the `create_qaoa_swap_circuit` function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk ini, kita boleh menggunakan kelas [`QAOAAnsatz`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.QAOAAnsatz) dari Qiskit. Kita memasukkan Circuit kosong ke medan `initial_state` dan `mixer_operator` untuk memastikan kita membina lapisan operator kos yang terpencil.\n"
"Kita juga mentakrifkan peta `edge_coloring` supaya gate RZZ diletakkan bersebelahan dengan gate SWAP. Penempatan strategik ini membolehkan kita mengeksploitasi pembatalan CX, mengoptimumkan Circuit untuk prestasi yang lebih baik.\n"
"Proses ini dilaksanakan dalam fungsi `create_qaoa_swap_circuit`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/82ae28b3-85eb-4487-8100-1e622e93cccf-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/82ae28b3-85eb-4487-8100-1e622e93cccf-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit Runtime primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-runtime-primitives}"
msgid "Step 3: Execute using IBM Quantum primitives {#step-3-execute-using-ibm-quantum-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Jalankan guna Qiskit Runtime primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-runtime-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's now prepare for hardware execution. Our first step will be to define a  Conditional Value at Risk (CVaR) cost function, which was introduced in [\\[3\\]](#references) for use within the paradigm of variational quantum optimization algorithms.\n"
msgstr "Mari kita sediakan untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan. Langkah pertama kita ialah menentukan fungsi kos Conditional Value at Risk (CVaR), yang diperkenalkan dalam [\\[3\\]](#references) untuk digunakan dalam paradigma algoritma pengoptimuman kuantum variasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CVaR of a random variable $X$ for a confidence level $α ∈ (0, 1]$ is defined as\n"
"$CVaR_{\\alpha}(X) = \\mathbb{E} \\lbrack X | X \\leq F_X^{-1}(\\alpha) \\rbrack$\n"
"where $F_X^{-1}(p)$ is the inverse cumulative distribution function of $X$. In other words, CVaR is the expected value of the lower $\\alpha$-tail of the distribution of $X$.\n"
msgstr ""
"CVaR bagi pemboleh ubah rawak $X$ untuk tahap keyakinan $α ∈ (0, 1]$ ditakrifkan sebagai\n"
"$CVaR_{\\alpha}(X) = \\mathbb{E} \\lbrack X | X \\leq F_X^{-1}(\\alpha) \\rbrack$\n"
"di mana $F_X^{-1}(p)$ ialah fungsi taburan kumulatif songsang bagi $X$. Dengan kata lain, CVaR ialah nilai jangkaan bagi ekor bawah $\\alpha$ daripada taburan $X$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The CVaR can be used as an error mitigation technique as previously discussed [\\[4\\]](#references). In this example, we determine $\\alpha$ and the number of shots according to the [error per layered gate](/guides/qpu-information#2q-error-layered) (EPLG) associated with the circuit.\n"
msgstr "CVaR boleh digunakan sebagai teknik pengurangan ralat seperti yang dibincangkan sebelum ini [\\[4\\]](#references). Dalam contoh ini, kita tentukan $\\alpha$ dan bilangan shots mengikut [error per layered gate](/guides/qpu-information#2q-error-layered) (EPLG) yang berkaitan dengan Circuit.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Proses lepas dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasikal yang dikehendaki {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's now visualize our results and then post-process them to find the value of the cut.\n"
msgstr "Mari kita visualisasikan hasil kita dan kemudian proses lepas untuk mencari nilai potongan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/761821cb-9a0c-4efb-806b-75513302d34a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/761821cb-9a0c-4efb-806b-75513302d34a-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following retrieves the best solution from the sampled bitstrings:\n"
msgstr "Berikut ini mengambil penyelesaian terbaik daripada bitstring yang disampelkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the Hamiltonian $H_C$ for the **max-cut** problem. Let each vertex of the graph be associated with a qubit in state $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$, where the value denotes the set the vertex is in. The goal of the problem is to maximize the number of edges $(v_1, v_2)$ for which $v_1 = |0\\rangle$ and $v_2 = |1\\rangle$, or vice versa. If we associate the $Z$ operator with each qubit, where\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan Hamiltonian $H_C$ untuk masalah **Max-Cut**. Biarkan setiap bucu graf dikaitkan dengan qubit dalam keadaan $|0\\rangle$ atau $|1\\rangle$, di mana nilai tersebut menandakan set yang dimiliki oleh bucu itu. Matlamat masalah ini ialah untuk memaksimumkan bilangan tepi $(v_1, v_2)$ di mana $v_1 = |0\\rangle$ dan $v_2 = |1\\rangle$, atau sebaliknya. Jika kita kaitkan operator $Z$ dengan setiap qubit, di mana\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"    Z|0\\rangle = |0\\rangle \\qquad Z|1\\rangle = -|1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"    Z|0\\rangle = |0\\rangle \\qquad Z|1\\rangle = -|1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then an edge $(v_1, v_2)$ belongs to the cut if the eigenvalue of $(Z_1|v_1\\rangle) \\cdot (Z_2|v_2\\rangle) = -1$; in other words, the qubits associated with $v_1$ and $v_2$ are different. Similarly, $(v_1, v_2)$ does not belong to the cut if the eigenvalue of $(Z_1|v_1\\rangle) \\cdot (Z_2|v_2\\rangle) = 1$.\n"
msgstr "maka tepi $(v_1, v_2)$ termasuk dalam potongan jika nilai eigen bagi $(Z_1|v_1\\rangle) \\cdot (Z_2|v_2\\rangle) = -1$; dengan kata lain, qubit yang dikaitkan dengan $v_1$ dan $v_2$ adalah berbeza. Begitu juga, $(v_1, v_2)$ tidak termasuk dalam potongan jika nilai eigen bagi $(Z_1|v_1\\rangle) \\cdot (Z_2|v_2\\rangle) = 1$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, let's draw a graph based on the CVaR result.\n"
"We split the graph nodes into two sets based on the CVaR result.\n"
"The nodes in the first set are colored in gray, and the nodes in the second set are colored in purple.\n"
"The edges between the two sets are the edges that are cut by the partitioning.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhir sekali, jom lukis graf berdasarkan hasil CVaR.\n"
"Kita bahagikan nod graf kepada dua set berdasarkan hasil CVaR.\n"
"Nod dalam set pertama diwarnakan kelabu, dan nod dalam set kedua diwarnakan ungu.\n"
"Tepi antara dua set tersebut ialah tepi yang dipotong oleh pembahagian itu.\n"

